  "uprn": "200003991952",
  "decision_date": "30/06/2005",
  "description": "Demolition of existing building and redevelopment of site with ten three-bedroom houses, one one-bedroom house and seven two-bedroom apartments with associated access and parking.",
  "site_name": "181-183",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "17/03/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "29/06/2010",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the accommodation is first occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 5 - The integral garages and car parking spaces shown on the submitted drawings shall be provided before the dwellings to which they relate are occupied and thereafter shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 6 - No construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Fridays and 8am to 1pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in the any wall or roof slope of the development hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 9 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external and internal noise transmission shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 11 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscaping and lighting have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Such details shall include, boundary treatment, parking layouts, vehicle access, separate pedestrian access and planting plans, and the scheme shall not be implemented otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.  The details so approved shall be implemented before first occupation of the properties or (in the case of planting ) in the first available planting season after completion of the development.",
    "Condition : 12 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before the dwellings hereby permitted are occupied. Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 13 - Before development commences details of sightlines at the point of access to the public highway shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall be carried out in accordance with the details.",
    "Condition : 14 - The development shall not be occupied until the easternmost access to the site is closed and reinstated so that it cannot be used as an access across the pavement.",
    "Condition : 15 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 16 - Before the development hereby permitted is commenced a scheme indicating the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to the ground floor flats shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use.",
    "Condition : 17 - Before the development is commenced a detailed site investigation shall be carried out to establish if the site is contaminated, to assess the degree and nature of the contamination present, and to determine its potential for the pollution of the water environment.  The method and extent of this site investigation shall be agreed with the Planning Authority prior to commencement of the work. Details of appropriate measures to prevent pollution of groundwater and surface water, including provisions for monitoring, shall then be submitted to and approved in writing by the Planning Authority before development commences. The development shall then proceed in strict accordance with the measures approved.",
    "Condition : 18 - No soakaways shall be constructed in contaminated ground.",
    "Condition : 19 - The construction of the foul and surface water drainage system shall be carried out in accordance with details submitted to and approved in writing by the Planning Authority before the development commences.",
    "Condition : 20 - The proposed redevelopment of the site for housing would be compatible with the character of the residential area and the proposal would not harm the appearance of the street scene or neighbours' living conditions. The development would provide acceptable living conditions, and would accord with the Council's traffic and parking standards. The proposal complies with policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), E.1.5 (Development involving Loss of or Changes in Employment Uses), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.4.2 (Residential Density) and T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities For Developments)."
